[38;5;231m⏺[39m I added a checkbox to the [38;5;153m<main>[39m element in [38;5;153mindex.html[39m:

  [90m<[34mlabel[90m>[39m
    [90m<[34minput[90m [36mtype[90m=[31m"checkbox"[90m [36mname[90m=[31m"done"[90m>[39m
    Mark as done
  [90m</[34mlabel[90m>[39m

  It's the browser's built-in checkbox, so clicking it switches between checked and unchecked without any JavaScript.
  Because the text is wrapped in the [38;5;153m<label>[39m, clicking "Mark as done" toggles the box too, and screen readers announce
  the checkbox with that text.

  Two things it doesn't do yet:
  - [1mThe state isn't saved.[0m Reloading the page clears it. Saving it would take a small amount of JavaScript, such as
    storing it in [38;5;153mlocalStorage[39m.
  - [1mThere's only one checkbox.[0m The page doesn't have a task list yet, so it isn't attached to any item. When you add
    tasks, put one of these next to each and change the text to the task's name.

  I haven't committed the change.

